  "question": {
    "text": "The value of the integral $\\int \\frac{d x}{\\left(e^x+e^{-x}\\right)^2}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\mathrm{e}^{2 \\mathrm{x}}+1\\right)+\\mathrm{C}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(e^{-2 x}+1\\right)+C$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-\\frac{1}{2}\\left(e^{2 x}+1\\right)^{-1}+C$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}\\left(e^{2 x}-1\\right)+C$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $\\int \\frac{e^{2 x} d x}{\\left(e^{2 x}+1\\right)^2} \\quad e^x=t ; e^x d x=d t$\n$$\n=\\frac{1}{2} \\int \\frac{2 \\mathrm{tdt}}{\\left(\\mathrm{t}^2+1\\right)^2}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left\\{-\\frac{1}{\\left(t^2+1\\right)}\\right\\}+c=-\\frac{1}{2\\left(\\mathrm{e}^{2 x}+1\\right)}+c\n$$"
  }
